# Accepted for a same-day demo that is destroyed after use. Both are real
# gaps, documented in README.md ("Azure variant" -> "Not hardened").
#
# AZU-0013: Key Vault accepts connections from any network. Access is still
#   gated by Entra ID + RBAC and logged. Locking it to a firewall would also
#   block Terraform on a laptop and the AKS pods without IP allow-lists or
#   private endpoints. Production: private endpoint + deny by default.
AZU-0013
# AZU-0041: the Kubernetes API server is reachable from any IP (still needs
#   credentials). GitHub-hosted runners use rotating IPs, so an allow-list
#   would break the deploy workflow. Production: private cluster + a
#   self-hosted runner inside the network.
AZU-0041
